  "query_preview": "/TUESDAY THROUGH SUNDAY/...\nIssued at 1231 AM MDT Mon Aug 17 2026\n\nModels continue to be in good agreement through the extended\nperiod, with NBM guidance starting to catch on to warmer\nconditions by late in the week into the weekend.  \n\nTuesday...upper level ridging continues ot build across southern\nColorado with warming temperatures and generally dry conditions\nacross the region. Temperatures will warm back through the 90s\nwith a few lower 100s possible near the Kansas border. PWAT\nvalues continue to dry out, and will help limit shower and\nthunderstorm activity. A couple of thunderstorms may be possible\nduring the afternoon and evening from the Central Mountains,\nsoutheast into teh Palmer Divide region as a weak wave tracks\nacross the area.\n\nWednesday...a cold front arrives by Wednesday morning turning \nlow level flow easterly by mid to late morning. Moisture returns\nas well with dewpoints reaching back into the upper 50s to \nlower 60s across the Plains. Shear also increases, with 0-6km \nshear values in excess of 30 kts by the afternoon. Expect \nshowers and thunderstorms to develop by early afternoon, \ninitially over the higher terrain, then spreading east into the \nPlains. As storms move into the Plains, a few could become \nstrong to severe with large hail and damaging winds possible. In\naddition, heavy rainfall will be possible, along with Flash \nFlooding on area burn scars. Temperatures will be cooler, with \n80s and lower 90s across the Plains. \n\nThursday through Sunday..models all in agreement with the upper\nhigh strengthening over the Great Basin, shifting east across\nColorado late in the week and over the weekend. Multiple waves\nembedded under the ridge will lift northward during this period,\nwith daily showers and thunderstorms possible. Most thunderstorm\nactivity will remain tied to the terrain, with a few slipping\neast into the I-25 corridor during the evening before\ndissipating. Extended NBM guidance is starting to catch up with\ndeterministic guidance on high temperatures Friday through\nSunday. Given the strength of the upper high, upper 90s to lower\n100s are not out of the question, especially for the weekend.",
